--- a/Help/cpack_gen/archive.rst	2026-11-10 03:32:26.419341011 -0600
+++ b/Help/cpack_gen/archive.rst	2026-11-10 04:02:39.355692594 -0600
@@ -174,6 +174,32 @@
 
   :Default: ``0`` (see policy :policy:`CMP0206`)
 
+.. variable:: CPACK_ARCHIVE_SORT_ENTRIES
+
+  .. versionadded:: 4.6
+
+  Write the archive's entries in name order. By default they follow the
+  order in which the staging directory was read, which on a filesystem with
+  hashed directories (such as ext4) differs from one filesystem to another,
+  so the same build on two machines produces two archives.
+
+  :Default: ``OFF``
+
+.. variable:: CPACK_ARCHIVE_UNAME
+              CPACK_ARCHIVE_GNAME
+
+  .. versionadded:: 4.6
+
+  Set the user and group NAME of entries contained in the archive. Set both
+  or neither. When unset, each entry records the name of the file's owner on
+  the machine that runs CPack, whatever :variable:`CPACK_ARCHIVE_UID` and
+  :variable:`CPACK_ARCHIVE_GID` say -- so two builders produce different
+  archives, and ``tar`` run as root, which restores ownership by name when a
+  name is present, gives the files to that user if the extracting machine has
+  one. ``root`` / ``root`` pairs with the default UID and GID of ``0``.
+
+  :Default: unset (the builder's names)
+
 Variables used by CPack Archive generator
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
